    "result_text": "I've implemented `complete_paragraph` in `app/tgi.py`. The existing test suite passes, but it only checks that the module imports. The function has never actually run, either against a real TGI server or a mocked one.\n\n- **Setup:** it creates `InferenceClient(model=endpoint_url)`, the same way `app/titles.py` does.\n- **The call:** `text_generation(prompt, max_new_tokens=200, stop=[\"\\n\\n\"], return_full_text=False)`.\n- **Return value:** the generated text with `.rstrip()` applied. TGI leaves the matched stop sequence at the end of the output, so the rstrip also removes the trailing `\"\\n\\n\"`.\n\n**Parameter name:** your pinned `huggingface-hub==2.0.0` calls the stop parameter `stop`, not `stop_sequences` like older versions and many examples do. The Context7 docs didn't list the parameters, so I read the signature in the installed library. I also set `return_full_text=False` explicitly, so the prompt is never included even if the server's default differs.\n\nNo dependencies were added."
